{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1376067-planning-a-chronicle-cabal-creation-process","id":1376067,"title":"Planning a Chronicle: Cabal Creation Process","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-03-21T22:15:22-07:00","id":1376067,"title":"Planning a Chronicle: Cabal Creation Process","content":"I've been taken in lately by some games with deeper worldbuilding and and intra-group dynamics, and want to bring a little of that into my next Mage game. I've thrown together an outline of questions and the like below, and am looking for a little input. The idea is to sort of &quot;make a house a home&quot; by freeing up the investment of personal Merit dots, getting players to think about the connections between a mage and her cabal and their sanctum, and hopefully breed a lot of ideas about how to get characters caught up in the world.<br /> <br /> Anyway, is this a thing? Just looking for tweaks, ideas, and inspiration. Thanks!<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Session Zero: Building the Cabal</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Instead of building a cabal around the individual characters, this method seeks to build a tightly-knit and established cabal invested in its community and its Sanctum. Characters are created after the Sanctum and cabal are created, and the process is meant to turn out cabals with detailed Sanctums, themed cabals, and politically active mages.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">From the Sanctum Out</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The players\u2019 first task, before building their characters, is to decide the nature of their Sanctum, and what sort of Mystery lays at its heart.</span></span><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Where is it? What sort of neighborhood is it?</li> <li>What kind of structure is it in?</li> <li>What\u2019s the Sanctum\u2019s known history?</li> <li>What\u2019s the Sanctum\u2019s reputation among its neighbors?</li> <li>What sort of special attention does it need?</li> <li>What mundane amenities does it have?</li> <li>What sort of arcane amenities does it have?</li> <li>What defenses does it have?</li> <li>What questions about the Sanctum remain?</li> <li> What is its name?</li> </ol><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Distribute </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>five to ten</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Merit dots among Safe Place, Sanctum, Hallow, and/or Library (normal or Advanced). The players may set aside dots for the Cabal phase.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Through the Cabal</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Players should have a rough idea of their characters before this point,</span></span><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>How long has the cabal resided in the Sanctum?</li> <li>How did they find the Sanctum?</li> <li>Why did they choose it to be their Sanctum?</li> <li>What sets the cabal apart from others in the Consilium?</li> <li>How expansive and organized is the cabal? (Retainer, Staff)</li> <li>What drew the cabal together?</li> <li>Who or what keeps it together now?</li> <li>Who or what has the cabal lost since its formation?</li> <li>How does the cabal deal with a crisis?</li> <li>What is the significance of the cabal, mystical, social, or otherwise? Does it have a theme?</li> </ol><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Each player assigns a single dot to one of the following Merits: Safe Space, Sanctum, Hallow, Library (normal or Advanced), Retainer, Staff,or Consilia Status (accorded to the cabal, any member may use it, but it does not stack with personal Status). If any dots were held over from the previous stage, distribute them now. </span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Into the Mage</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Players now build their characters with the above in mind. Any player may add their own Merit dots to the shared Merits above (with the exception of Consilium Status), instead of to their own character.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Once the characters are finished and introduced to the other players, each player takes a turn describing one good or bad experience between their mage and another player\u2019s, and to what degree it affects their relationship. The chosen character must be one that hasn\u2019t been picked yet. Any player can veto or modify or expand an experience that diverges from their character\u2019s concept, of course. Finally, each player describes a Mystery their character is investigating.</span></span><br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-22T14:35:35-07:00","id":1376154,"title":"","content":"I like it this idea a lot, it makes the Sanctum into a place where the cabal can take a breather from the world. Its also a group project they can bond over. Some things to keep in mind:<br /> <br /> 1- Try not to tell the entire political background at once, it can be a lot to absorb at the start. Give them the top layer of why they have it and let them explore the depths as they go.<br /> <br /> 2- The Mystery could present itself as they go. For example, the Consilium gave them a good Sanctum because they had a deal with the Iron Master werewolf gangsters. The Lex Magicka ratified it and placed the obligation on whatever cabal owned it. Or there is an old mage's study hidden within or some kind of ruin. But be sure to compartmentize the issue so you don't drive them away from the Sanctum.<br /> <br /> 3- Make a bowl with papers saying things like &quot;you were drunk and cabalmate X shared a secret with each other, what was it ?&quot; or &quot;you had an argument with cabalmate Y last week, what was it about ?&quot;. Draw one or two per person to improvise a cabal background. That way you can break the ice between the characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 03-22-2020, 06:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-22T17:00:25-07:00","id":1376176,"title":"","content":"My current D&amp;D group ran a session 0 deriving from Kids On Bikes, which has a similar feel to 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-23T05:35:51-07:00","id":1376246,"title":"","content":"Very nice. The only thing I\u2019d add is to ask the players why they chose to settle here. Mages are capable of being highly mobile so they are likely to go to the kinds of places that further their Obsessions. Answering that question will get them invested in your setting and its central Mystery.<br /> <br /> Answering that question for your NPCs is also useful for figuring out your cast population and motives, and creating plot hooks for your cabal to engage with.<br /> <br /> For instance everyone in London should be interested in the Rune Walks for one reason or other. They trade routes, or knife someone for their archives, want a boost to a particular goal and think the Rune Walks can get them to the right level, or just like exploring and documenting the weirdness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 03-23-2020, 08:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-23T06:20:20-07:00","id":1376252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1376067-planning-a-chronicle-cabal-creation-process?p=1376176#post1376176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My current D&amp;D group ran a session 0 deriving from Kids On Bikes, which has a similar feel to 3.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool, the idea for 3 came from a pretty interesting system used to run D&amp;D:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/vKQv4GC0N9Q\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/vKQv4GC0N9Q\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/vKQv4GC0N9Q\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/vKQv4GC0N9Q </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It doesn't translate 1 to 1 into Mage, but it has some pretty interesting dynamic worldbuilding ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"